# Monorepo Migration Guardrails

Applies during M1–M6 migration work. Source: `docs/migration-plan.md`, ADR-003, REQ-016.

## Non-Negotiables

1. **No product feature rewrites** (REQ-016) — move code, fix imports, update CI/deploy wiring only.
2. **Vendor is read-only** — `vendor/schemas/*` content comes from wmo-im sync PRs only.
3. **GIFTs upstream is manual** (REQ-014, ADR-004) — no scheduled Action for mgoberfield/GIFTs.
4. **Two deployables post-migration** — API (backend+auth) + static frontend; no separate auth service.
5. **Big-bang cutover** — single PR removes `.gitmodules`; no long-lived dual layout.

## Submodule → Target Mapping

| Current | Target | Strategy |
|---------|--------|----------|
| `schemas/iwxxm` | `vendor/schemas/iwxxm` | wmo-im snapshot |
| `schemas/iwxxm-codelists` | `vendor/schemas/iwxxm-codelists` | snapshot |
| `schemas/iwxxm-modelling` | `vendor/schemas/iwxxm-modelling` | snapshot |
| `data/iwxxm-translation` | `vendor/schemas/iwxxm-translation` | snapshot |
| `GIFTs/` | `packages/gifts/` | full source |
| `frontend/` | `apps/frontend/` | full source |
| `auth/` | `packages/auth/` + routes in `apps/backend/` | library merge |
| `backend/` | `apps/backend/` | move + wire workspace deps |

## Migration Acceptance

Before marking M1 complete:
- `.gitmodules` absent (TC-M004)
- `git clone` works without `--recurse-submodules` (UJ-DEV-001)
- Golden conversion outputs unchanged (TC-M003)
- Auth on backend host; docker-compose has two app services (TC-M005)

Raise `[Scope Drift]` for new product features disguised as migration work.
